+// ===== AI(W906-ST01C) 20261005: the NOT 910 helpers of this file (declared in atester_FinePitch.h / the head block) =====
+//  Steven 1005 23:2x (Q-R5): 「我們的馬達是class概念，可以使用多種不同的軸卡或是ethercat通訊或是motionnet ... 不應該糾結在1203」 ⇒ none of these
+//  helpers is keyed on a card type or a Model string: they are live whenever this flow runs in a SHIP build (the flow's only
+//  caller-to-be is the Type_HT9050 Index slot, slice 2) and read the Index Z1 MOTOR OBJECT through its class interface
+//  (TMyMotor -> Motor: HTMotor*; the Index axes' API is Gali_* when INDEX_MOTION_CARD==0, cinitial.cpp InitialMotorParameter).
+//  SOFT_SIMULTE: inert (golden's simulated motors).  None blocks a stop.
+//  Existing PCI1203-keyed helpers that are REUSED as is (E-042 / E-044, on main / in !218): W906_IndexZDriveFault (P7's 1203 part:
+//  monitor / sample / route health), W906_Ht9050TorqueWaitTimedOut (E-044), and the E-038 torque bridge behind COM2->ReadTorque.
+static bool FP9050ProtectLive()
+{
+#ifdef SOFT_SIMULTE
+    return false;
+#else
+    return true;
+#endif
+}
+static bool FP9050IndexOnGalilApi() { return INDEX_MOTION_CARD==0; }   // golden's own selector of the Index axes' class (TMyGALILMotor)
+int W906_FP9050LeafCount = 0;
+static bool FP9050Leaf(const char* what)
+{
