+//  F1 in class terms (motor-control skill, motor-classes.md): with INDEX_MOTION_CARD==0 golden builds the Index axes as
+//  TMyGALILMotor (cinitial.cpp InitialMotorParameter) and drives them only through TMyMotor's Galil API (Gali_MotMove /
+//  Gali_ReadPos ...): that API is what reaches a DMC card, the Galil route (HT9050: PCIE-1203, Motor/GaliRoute.h) or golden's no-card
+//  simulation, and it keeps the Galil sign convention (Position = -flow).  910's plain MOT[MTestZ1].ReadPos() / MotorMove go to
+//  HTMotor::ReadPos / MoveToPos of TMyGALILMotor, which need a DMC card (bGali_CardInstall): 0 / no motion otherwise.
+//  Index axes on another HTMotor class (INDEX_MOTION_CARD!=0): 910's ReadPos / MotorMove, unchanged.
+int W906_FP9050Z1Pos()
+{
+    if(FP9050IndexOnGalilApi())
+        return (int)MOT[MTestZ1].Gali_ReadPos();
+    return MOT[MTestZ1].ReadPos();
+}
